On Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:07:30 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> Can we simplify this? I don't think I want a `just archive` task that I
> have to run manually.
>
> I would like to automatically move the file into the archive dir if I
> apply the archive tag.

Yes. Posted as "[PATCH] emacs: Archive notmuch mail by moving its
file" [1]. There is no just task and no separate request tag any more.
The archived tag is the operation.

notmuch-archive-tags is now ("-inbox" "+archived"). A function on
notmuch-after-tag-hook watches for archived being added or removed.
Adding it moves the message's file from cur/ or new/ into
maildir/archive/. Removing it moves the file back to cur/. Either way
the function then runs notmuch new, so mail-tag.sh re-derives the tags
from where the file now lives.

> Essentially I want two operations to run in notmuch-emacs: archive and
> unarchive. archive moves the file into the archive dir, and unarchive
> moves it out.
>
> I don't know if this is best done by just applying the tag, or by
> having a dedicated operation.

I went with the tag. "a" archives and C-u a unarchives, the stock
notmuch-emacs keys and their prefix convention. Because the hook fires
on every tag change made through notmuch-emacs, it covers "a" on a
single message, "A" on a thread, "a" on a search result or region, and
"+archived" or "-archived" by hand. A dedicated command would have to
re-implement each of those.

> I am making an intentional action to archive or unarchive, and that
> should have the effect of files being moved to the appropriate location
> and being tagged correctly.

The file moves when you press the key, and the tags come from the
reindex that follows. If a tag change can't match a move, such as on a
draft, notmuch new reverts it, so the database never disagrees with the
maildir. You commit the moves in mail.jj as before.

The patch needs "notmuch: Tag messages under archive/ as archived" [2]
for the derived tags. It replaces "[PATCH v2] mail: Add just
archive" [3] and "[PATCH 0/2] Archive from notmuch-emacs with the
archive tag" [4], so please drop both. That also drops the drafts fix I
promised for a v3 of [3], since the just task is gone.

Patch 2 of "[PATCH v2 0/2] Archive messages that need no answer" [5]
still documents a manual mv into maildir/archive/cur/. That is stale
twice over, since the layout is flat and archiving now happens in
emacs. I'll revise it if you want that series kept.

